(* Home page *****************************************************************)
^pageWithImages{Home}{^T{Gauge One Model Railway Association home page}}{^homePrimary}{^empty}
{^image{home1_^lang.jpg}{David Viewing's Locomotion No 1}}{^image{home1_^lang.jpg}{David Viewing's Locomotion No 1}}		{^image{home3_^lang.jpg}{Accucraft Class 66}}
{
 ^hbox{
  ^tbox{^h1{^T{Welcome to the Gauge One Model Railway Association}}
   ^PAR{
    ^T{Gauge 1 model railways run on tracks where the rails are 45mm or 1¾ inches apart. For standard gauge, this corresponds to a scale of 1:32 or around 10mm to the foot.}

    ^T{We run models powered by on-board batteries, by track-supplied current and by live steam with boilers fired by alcohol, gas or coal. Even clockwork engines still make occasional appearances.}

        ^cbox{
           ^PAR{^T{The size of Gauge 1 models allows for exquisite levels of detail in fine-scale models, and the availability of robust, simplified models also makes it an ideal scale for youngsters. You can read about the breadth of activity within G1MRA by downloading these copies of our welcome brochure and our quarterly magazine.}}
           ^hgap
           ^link{^img{welcomeToGauge1.jpg}{Front cover image of welcome brochure}}{images/Recruiting-brochure-7.pdf}
           ^hgap
           ^link{^img{G1MRA_229_cover.jpg}{Front cover image of magazine issue 229}}{images/G1MRA_229.pdf}
           ^hgap	
        }

    ^PAR{^T{There are around 2,000 G1MRA members spread across 23 countries. Around two thirds of the membership are UK based with the remainder mostly in Europe and North America. 

We are a very sociable bunch. Much of our activity centres on running sessions held in members' gardens where you will meet both newcomers and experienced hands: an enthusiastic and knowledgeable community which shares expertise ranging from 130 year old clockwork design and live steam through to the most modern 3D printing and computer-based control techniques. 

^bf{New members are always welcome: see ^link{this page}{Join^us^lang.html} for details.}}}
   }
  }   
  ^fill       
  ^sbox{
   <h1><a href="Events_^lang.html" style="color:#165f4b;">Events</a></h1>
   ^homeEvents
   ^hrule
   ^h1{^link{More events}{events_^lang.html}}
  }
 }
}

(* Events pages **************************************************************) 
(* ^homeEvents, ^futureEvents and ^pastEvents are defined in events.amp *)
^pageWithImages{Events}{^T{Gauge One Model Railway Association events page}}{^eventsPrimary}{^eventsSecondary}{^image{events1_^lang.jpg}{1}}{^image{events2_^lang.jpg}{2}}{^image{events3_^lang.jpg}{3}}{	
^cbox{^tbox{^h1{^T{Events}}^PAR{^T{G1MRA organises a public Spring meeting and an Autumn AGM and exhibition each year. We attend other public shows by invitation, often with one of our portable tracks.

G1MRA groups also arrange numerous members-only meetings, many of which are in private gardens. This is a public website, so we do not publish names or addresses for these events here. To find out about activities in your area, locate your nearest group from ^link{this list}{groups_^lang.html} and then email that group's contact quoting your membership number. You may also email the G1MRA committee officer for groups as ^g1mail{groups}.

You will find information about recent past events on ^link{this page}{Past_^lang.html}.

^bf{If you have an event that you would like to add to this list, please complete ^link{this form}{^newEventForm}}.
^vskip
}}^homeEvents^futureEvents}
}}

